mes New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.71%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_WjgvnHt0q0K__9ck3rxJew" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PropertyPlantAndEquipmentNet" scale="0" id="Tc_Kd5q617GrUukSeISF2YrQw_8_6">60,769</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">Depreciation expense for the&#160;years ended June 30, 2026 and 2025 was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_TTMuJ8akHEyNSbvl-jNDpg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="0" id="Narr_hrUWOe_m4ECyPkydF-kRMQ">44,515</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2024_To_6_30_2025_FKyOfCPQK0m44cvkPkH5TQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="0" id="Narr_-svg_cFWmkuZzc4mQ4dBFg">43,899</ix:nonFraction>, respectively.</p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><a id="Tc_sNiSWF8dEES9KFp5pXGIvw_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_oGO8C7cnAEiBhBTIdkYciA_1_5"></a><a id="Tc_ebhNpduY1U-R8NRGStF1MQ_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_aje-K53bxECNARbw_MFBqg_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_BqCYYmr2FEC2d1M-rcpKIQ_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_QebqOo0eQE-zyDgH8xGoQQ_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_ZXChXWyWi0a1QbjF--51vg_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_e65HC6rEdk-KOpYQDbDhIA_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_NBqpxATqSkqiKwtWh0JBSQ_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_fE-BfqI3WkmMLrwsLax_cw_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_jEUDuaI-8kGiaj4oCglYjQ_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_zixQ6bK4EE-0HV6xe_NPow_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_ze4KctFyKkekEQYdfHOn-g_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_vcomJsWh0kKvOoXIhB7a4A_10_0"></a><a id="Tc_pnGWDTCbT0y03Kb-wHwX4Q_11_0"></a><a id="Tc_5HdbRYVEek-WoSyxut3Jew_12_0"></a><a id="Tc_-TwFsIbngk2tdYSKmG31tQ_13_0"></a><a id="Tc_rgZb7-FIe0G8orRmtyaynw_13_2"></a><a id="Tc_yBbZDqUv0UqtYfmAi7Ht3g_13_5"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_TTMuJ8akHEyNSbvl-jNDpg" name="us-gaap:IntangibleAssetsDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_xSMp-2-r40K1Z68HQFtyrQ" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt;">Note&#160;4.&#160;&#160;&#160;Intangible Assets</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">Intangible assets consist of developed technology, customer relationships, customer lists and intellectual property licenses acquired in prior acquisitions and are stated at cost less accumulated amortization. The developed technology, customer relationships and customer lists are being amortized over the estimated useful lives of <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_9XowhKGGMk-mD0oHbqJMhQ" format="ixt-sec:duryear" name="us-gaap:FiniteLivedIntangibleAssetUsefulLife" id="Narr_2xqjHWCx1UCmNIpY-NO68g">3</ix:nonNumeric> to <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_6Nporu0OB02HTYjjVPoe7Q" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="us-gaap:FiniteLivedIntangibleAssetUsefulLife" id="Narr_p15BcHNUJ0KSyGPhwgpflw">10 years</ix:nonNumeric>. The Company does not have any intangible assets deemed to have indefinite lives. Amortization expense for the years ended June 30, 2026 and 2025 was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_TTMuJ8akHEyNSbvl-jNDpg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfIntangibleAssets" scale="0" id="Narr_8JYVZq0F20uX7QCugtg5sA">1,201,458</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2024_To_6_30_2025_FKyOfCPQK0m44cvkPkH5TQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfIntangibleAssets" scale="0" id="Narr_aNgy6ML_b0CO8QhK_Bzgag">1,201,463</ix:nonFraction>, respectively. Amortization expense expected to be recognized is approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_lGfTMIk8U02KeD9zfct_bg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FiniteLivedIntangibleAssetsAmortizationExpenseNextTwelveMonths" scale="0" id="Narr_FeLUFFhuqUyN1x0sqo6Fqg">1,173,000</ix:nonFraction> annually in 2027 through 2031 and approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_dWw5jbCz-0q4_XMGyHpImQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_lGfTMIk8U02KeD9zfct_bg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FiniteLivedIntangibleAssetsAmortizationExpenseAfterYearFive" scale="0" id="Narr_i4aB7RfjXEeYy9XaeC5w4w">2,670,000</ix:nonFraction> thereafter.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">Intangible assets consist of the following as of June 30, 2026 and 2025:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_TTMuJ8akHEyNSbvl-jNDpg" 